WEBVTT

NOTE Captions placed above the English text already embedded in the video.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500 line:8%
What is MED13 syndrome?
A journey from the human body into our DNA.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.500 line:8%
Some children are born with a very rare genetic condition
called MED13 syndrome.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.900 line:8%
To understand it, let's travel inside the body.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.900 line:8%
Our bodies are built from trillions of cells. Almost every cell
carries the same instruction book: our DNA.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.900 line:8%
MED13 syndrome mainly affects the developing brain:
how a child learns, moves and communicates.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.900 line:8%
The brain has billions of nerve cells. Inside each one
is a control center called the nucleus.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:55.900 line:8%
The nucleus holds our DNA, packed into 46 chromosomes:
23 from each parent.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.900 line:8%
On chromosome 17, at a spot scientists call 17q23.2,
sits a gene named MED13.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.900 line:8%
DNA is a code written with just four letters:
A, T, C and G.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.900 line:8%
A gene is one recipe in that code. The MED13 recipe
tells the cell how to build the MED13 protein.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:26.900 line:8%
The MED13 protein works in a team called the Mediator.
Together they act like a dimmer switch.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.900 line:8%
They help set which genes turn on, when, and how strongly.
That timing is vital as the brain develops.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.900 line:8%
In MED13 syndrome, one of a child's two copies of the MED13 gene
has a change, often in just one letter.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.900 line:8%
In most children (92%) the change is brand new,
not passed down from a parent. Nothing the parents did caused it.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.900 line:8%
Scientists think that with the switch out of balance,
genes that guide brain development are set to the wrong level.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.900 line:8%
Every child with MED13 syndrome is different,
but many share some common features.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.900 line:8%
And behind every diagnosis is a child
with their own personality, strengths and joys.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:21.900 line:8%
MED13 syndrome was first described in 2018. More than
200 people have now been identified worldwide.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.900 line:8%
The MED13 Foundation brings families, researchers
and clinicians together.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.900 line:8%
Together we are accelerating discovery, funding research
toward treatments, and supporting every family.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.900 line:8%
Learn more, join the research cohort,
and support the mission at med13.org.